NAME
     nsenter - run a program in another process's namespaces

SYNOPSIS
     nsenter -t PID [-a] [-u] [-p] [-m] [-U] [-n] [COMMAND [ARG...]]

DESCRIPTION
     nsenter joins the namespaces of the process named by -t and runs
     COMMAND there -- which is how to look inside a container from
     outside it.

OPTIONS
     -t PID   whose namespaces to join
     -a       all of them
     -u       the hostname namespace
     -p       the process-number namespace
     -m       the mount namespace
     -U       the user namespace
     -n       the network namespace

SEE ALSO
     unshare(1), vmm(1)
